      "summary": "The kingdom was carved out of the fertile agricultural heartland of the Zingg Valley, established as a regal gift to the youngest son of the high monarch. In its early centuries, the nascent realm flourished into an independent and prosperous power, celebrated for its devotion to innovative learning, architectural wonder, and deep arcane research. Yet even in this golden dawn, a dark shadow was cast: a foul sorcerer invoked unspeakable eldritch rites to forge an indestructible weapon—the Black Blade of Azur. Upon the discovery of his vile crimes, the sorcerer was executed, and the indestructible blade was sealed deep within an underground crypt beneath the valley to forever isolate its corrupting influence from mankind.",
      "content": "\n<div class=\"info-card\">\n  <p><strong>Chronological Designation:</strong> Period I: The Gift</p>\n  <p><strong>Core Theme:</strong> Founding of the Realm & The Buried Blade</p>\n</div>\n<h3>Historical Chronicle</h3>\n<p>The kingdom was carved out of the fertile agricultural heartland of the <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#gazetteer/zingg-valley\">Zingg Valley</a>, established as a regal gift to the youngest son of the high monarch. In its early centuries, the nascent realm flourished into an independent and prosperous power, celebrated for its devotion to innovative learning, architectural wonder, and deep arcane research. Yet even in this golden dawn, a dark shadow was cast: a foul sorcerer invoked unspeakable eldritch rites to forge an indestructible weapon—the <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#relics/black-blade\">Black Blade of Azur</a>. Upon the discovery of his vile crimes, the sorcerer was executed, and the indestructible blade was sealed deep within an underground crypt beneath the valley to forever isolate its corrupting influence from mankind.</p>\n\n",
