      "summary": "Subterranean Sunken Ruins. Black markets, hidden refuges, ancient artifacts.",
      "content": "\n<div class=\"info-card\">\n  <p><strong>Geographical Type:</strong> Subterranean Sunken Ruins</p>\n  <p><strong>Strategic &amp; Economic Value:</strong> Black markets, hidden refuges, ancient artifacts.</p>\n  <p><strong>Primary Encounter Hazards:</strong> Criminal syndicates, rogue zombies, toxic cave-ins, stone guardians.</p>\n</div>\n<h3>Geographical Description</h3>\n<p><a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#relics/final-guard\">The Final Guard</a>: Kalenius's mausoleum is permanently guarded by the <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#relics/final-guard\">Final Guard</a>—one thousand elite ancient Thurian warriors transformed into deathless, animate stone.</p>\n<p>4.2 Interior Fiefs & Agricultural Heartland</p>\n\n<div class=\"gm-callout\">\n  <div class=\"gm-badge\">GM CONFIDENTIAL &bull; REGIONAL HAZARDS &amp; HOOKS</div>\n  <p><strong>Encounter Threats:</strong> Criminal syndicates, rogue zombies, toxic cave-ins, stone guardians.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>The Underworld Dens: The Cistern of the Blind Saint</h3>\n<p>Deep beneath the ruined sunken palaces of The Pit, beyond the patrols of <a href=\"#factions/republican-insurgents\" class=\"wiki-link\">Republican Insurgents</a> and the zombie containment pits, lies the secret heart of Kordova's criminal empire: <strong>The Cistern of the Blind Saint</strong>. A colossal pre-Cataclysmic reservoir carved from black granite during Period II, this subterranean vault serves as the headquarters of <a href=\"#factions/kordovan-thieves-guild\" class=\"wiki-link\">The Night Guild of Kordova</a>. From an elevated dais above the dark waters, <a href=\"#npcs/beltran-desoto\" class=\"wiki-link\">Guildmaster Don Beltrano de Zoto</a> administers <em>El <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#overview/pundonor\">Pundonor</a> del Arroyo</em>, adjudicating criminal disputes, storing fenced silver, and coordinating defenses against <a href=\"#factions/velasco-thieves-guild\" class=\"wiki-link\">Velascan cutthroats</a> seeking to infiltrate the depths.</p>\n\n<p><strong><a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#gazetteer/royal-university-of-kordava\">The University</a> Scriptorium Outfall:</strong> Directly above the northern rim of The Pit loom the crumbling foundations of <a href=\"#gazetteer/royal-university-of-kordava\" class=\"wiki-link\">The Royal University of Kordava</a>. Flooded drainage conduits and ancient elven cisterns beneath the Sunken Scriptorium descend straight into the upper levels of The Pit, providing a covert smuggling conduit utilized by <a href=\"#npcs/eusebio-falcon\" class=\"wiki-link\">Maestro Eusevios</a> and underworld scavengers from the <a href=\"#factions/kordovan-thieves-guild\" class=\"wiki-link\">Night Guild</a>.</p>\n\n<h3>The Sunken City of Kordava (Wagner's 'Road of Kings')</h3>\n<p>As depicted in Karl Edward Wagner's <em>Conan: The Road of Kings</em>, modern <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#gazetteer/kordava\">Kordava</a> was constructed directly upon the colossal, earthquake-shattered ruins of the ancient pre-Cataclysmic metropolis. Far beneath the cobblestones of the Grand Plaza and the High Alcázar lies <strong>The Pit</strong>—a multi-tiered subterranean underworld where ancient Thurian and Acheronian architecture mingles with stagnant flood-waters, smugglers' canals, and secret revolutionary armories.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>The Upper Sump:</strong> Home to illegal distilleries, fencing dens like <a href=\"#gazetteer/the-drowned-rat\" class=\"wiki-link\">The Drowned Rat</a>, and black-market stalls run by <a href=\"#npcs/vesper\" class=\"wiki-link\">Vesper the Key-Master</a>.</li>\n  <li><strong>The Middle Vaults (The Rose Canton):</strong> The fortified redoubt of <a href=\"#factions/republican-insurgents\" class=\"wiki-link\">The Rebels of the White Rose</a>, featuring hidden dueling salles, bomb-making workshops, and secret passageways leading into palace cellars.</li>\n  <li><strong>The Deep Abysses:</strong> Cyclopean pre-human masonry holding the slumbering stone warriors of the <a href=\"#relics/final-guard\" class=\"wiki-link\">Final Guard of King Kalenius</a> and forgotten tombs guarding ancient relics.</li>\n</ul>\n",
