      "summary": "Independent captains, corsairs, and privateers with letters of marque.",
      "content": "\n<div class=\"info-card\">\n  <p><strong>Faction Classification:</strong> Corsairs of the Baracha Strait</p>\n</div>\n<h3>Faction Dossier &amp; Operations</h3>\n<p>Independent captains, corsairs, and privateers with letters of marque.</p>\n<p>Plunder merchant lanes, control Baracha Strait, extort coastal towns.</p>\n<p>Lack of central discipline; easily swayed by plunder or mutiny.</p>\n<p>Maritime hazards, extortionists, or deniable covert mercenaries.</p>\n\n\n<h3>The Zingaran Corsairs vs. Barachan Freebooters</h3>\n<p>Within the treacherous waters of the Barachan archipelago, a fierce cultural and naval rivalry exists between two distinct factions of reavers:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>The Proud Zingaran Buccaneers:</strong> Commanded by aristocratic captains such as <a href=\"#npcs/zaporavo\" class=\"wiki-link\">Captain Zaporavo</a> of the <em>Wastrel</em> and <a href=\"#npcs/zarono\" class=\"wiki-link\">Captain Black Zarono</a>, these privateers man their caravels exclusively with Zingaran sailors, observing strict chivalric etiquette, fighting formal rapier duels, and sailing under royal or Grandee letters of marque.</li>\n  <li><strong>The Freebooters of Baracha:</strong> Led by rough foreign sea-wolves like Strombanni and the daring renegade <a href=\"#npcs/gonzago\" class=\"wiki-link\">Captain Gonzago</a> of <em><a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#npcs/casimiro-velasco\">The Hawk</a></em>, operating out of fortified pirate islands and preying upon merchant traffic from Zingara, <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#factions/foreign-powers\">Argos</a>, and Stygia.</li>\n  <li><strong>The Legend of <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#relics/treasure-of-tranicos\">Tranicos</a>:</strong> All corsairs share a burning, feverish obsession with locating <a href=\"#relics/treasure-of-tranicos\" class=\"wiki-link\">The Lost Treasure of Tranicos</a>, hidden in the fog-bound sea caves of the northern coast.</li>\n</ul>\n",
