      "summary": "Terrifying necromantic conduit uncovered by Mad King Daedalus. Grants supreme command over undead hordes, buried with Daedalus beneath The Pit.",
      "content": "\n<h3>7.2 The Obsidian Blade</h3>\n<div class=\"info-card\">\n  <p><strong>Historical Origin:</strong> Uncovered by <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#history/daedalus\">Mad King Daedalus</a> in Period V to channel the sacrificial blood of citizens and envoys into his cauldron for godhood.</p>\n  <p><strong>Current Status:</strong> Buried deep within the smoldering rubble of old <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#gazetteer/kordava\">Kordava</a> beneath <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#gazetteer/the-pit\">The Pit</a>, where <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#history/daedalus\">King Daedalus</a> lies eternally trapped by <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#history/tanatos\">Tanatos</a>.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>Eldritch Properties &amp; Powers</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Horde Command:</strong> The wielder can mentally command hundreds of memory-retaining thralls simultaneously over miles without verbal orders.</li>\n  <li><strong>Mass Exhumation:</strong> Plunging the blade into unhallowed ground automatically animates fallen corpses within a 300-foot radius.</li>\n  <li><strong>The Cosmic Curse:</strong> The blade constantly whispers with the voices of <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#history/daedalus\">Daedalus</a> and the victims of the Starfall. Wielding it requires a Save vs. Spells every dawn or suffer paranoid megalomania.</li>\n</ul>\n",
      "gmSecrets": "If the blade is taken from Daedalus's hand, Tanatos's imprisonment ritual will collapse.",
