      "summary": "Don Tristao de Revello's proposed reinstatement has drawn competing claims to Revella.",
      "content": "<h3>Current situation</h3><p><a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#npcs/tristan-revella\">Don Tristao de Revello</a>'s proposed reinstatement has drawn competing claims to <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#gazetteer/revella\">Revella</a>. Sixty miners and deserters of La Hermandad del Pico, led by Toribio the Anvil, hold the mines and reject renewed serfdom. Tristao has pledged mineral rights to <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#npcs/demetrio-phokas\">Demetrio Phokas</a>, <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#npcs/beltran-desoto\">Don Beltrano</a> de Zoto, and Sadoria's clerks. <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#npcs/gonzalo-guarralid\">Duke Gonzalgo</a> disputes his title through retainers and a champion. Tristao's drinking and fear of the flooded Black Shaft undermine his ambitions. Black Tin resonates with a buried entity; miners report sleepwalking and geometric frost on ingots. The university wants dependable tin supplies, adding another interested party to the dispute.</p>",
