      "content": "<h3>Current situation</h3><p><a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#npcs/andres-hojeda\">Androvo de Ojedo</a> holds Rodorigo's original Period VII Dispatch of the Black River, ordering the murder of thirty church peace emissaries and the planting of republican pamphlets. He refused the order and fled with the parchment, now hidden in a lead case in the chapel altar at <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#gazetteer/san-severo\">San Severo</a>. Rodorigo's hound-masters and caballeros have orders to burn the chapel and silence its occupants during the assault. Sadoria wants the document for his own leverage. Its exposure threatens the general, but the loyalty of his cavalry and the credibility of witnesses remain political questions. This is distinct from the Period VI assassination evidence held by republican cells.</p>",
