      "summary": "The fiercely proud, volatile Zingaran buccaneer captain of the famed privateer caravel The Wastrel. A flamboyant master of the rapier who dresses in slashed scarlet silks, a feathered velvet bonnet, and gold hoops, commanding an all-Zingaran crew in the Barachan waters with tyrannical punctilio and deadly skill.",
      "atAGlance": {
        "Visual Appearance": "A slender, sinewy Zingaran dressed in slashed scarlet and violet silks, a gold-embroidered velvet bonnet tilted rakishly with a tall black egret plume, heavy gold hoops in his ears, and a pointed beard black as pitch, scented with exotic spikenard.",
        "Demeanor & Mannerisms": "Haughty, mercurial, and hyper-sensitive about his pedigree. Touches the filigreed basket-hilt of his rapier whenever addressed by commoners; laughs softly before killing; enforces rigid naval discipline among his crew.",
        "Combat Style": "Peerless Zingaran duelist (10th-Level Swashbuckler). Fights with lightning rapier thrusts and an off-hand parrying dagger, utilizing acrobatic footwork, deck rigging, and feints to disarm and skewer foes.",
        "Social Lever": "Pundonor obsession. He considers himself a knight-errant of the sea; questioning his chivalric birth or his ship's honor guarantees an immediate challenge to single combat at dawn."
      },
      "content": "\n<div class=\"npc-header-card\">\n  <div class=\"npc-meta\">\n    <span class=\"badge faction-badge\"><a href=\"#factions/barachan-pirates\" class=\"wiki-link\">Barachan Pirates & Freebooters</a> / Privateers</span>\n    <span class=\"badge rival-badge\">Rivals: <a href=\"#npcs/zarono\" class=\"wiki-link\">Captain Black Zarono</a> & <a href=\"#npcs/gonzago\" class=\"wiki-link\">Captain Gonzago</a></span>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"at-a-glance-grid\">\n    <div class=\"glance-item\"><strong>Visual Appearance:</strong> A slender, sinewy Zingaran aristocrat dressed in slashed scarlet and violet silks, a gold-embroidered velvet bonnet with a tall black egret plume, heavy gold hoops, and a pointed beard scented with exotic oils.</div>\n    <div class=\"glance-item\"><strong>Demeanor & Mannerisms:</strong> Haughty, mercurial, and intensely proud. Demands royal punctilio aboard ship; speaks in elevated courtly Zingaran; will execute a sailor for failing to salute his quarterdeck.</div>\n    <div class=\"glance-item\"><strong>Combat Style:</strong> 10th-Level Swashbuckler/Fighter. Lightning rapier lunges and main-gauche parries. AC -1 in dueling silks; attacks twice per round with masterwork blade <em>Wind of <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#gazetteer/kordava\">Kordava</a></em> (+3 to hit, 1d8+5 damage).</div>\n    <div class=\"glance-item\"><strong>Social Lever:</strong> Extreme vulnerability to <em>pundonor</em> insults. He refuses to take orders from the <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#factions/restoration-council\">Restoration Council</a>, but can be lured into parley by appealing to his chivalric knightly lineage.</div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<h3>Dossier & Narrative Lore</h3>\n<p><strong>The Terror of the Barachan Waters.</strong> First chronicled in Robert E. Howard's canonical tale <em>\"The Pool of the Black One\"</em>, Captain Zaporavo represents the zenith of Zingaran maritime chivalry curdled into ruthless piracy. Disowned from a noble Kordovan lineage following a blood feud, Zaporavo took to the high seas aboard the <em>Wastrel</em>—a sleek, double-banked caravel built in the naval yards of <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#gazetteer/kordava\">Kordava</a>. Unlike the drunken multinational scum who man Barachan pirate vessels under foreign captains like Strombanni, Zaporavo's crew is composed strictly and exclusively of Zingarans: disgraced noble duelists, exiled caballeros, and hardened sea-wolves who observe a savage parody of chivalric etiquette.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Captive of <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#gazetteer/kordava\">Kordava</a>.</strong> Zaporavo's pride and cruelty are legendary. Having raided a Grandee coastal pleasure-galley off the Vega of <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#gazetteer/kordava\">Kordava</a>, he carried off the noblewoman <a href=\"#npcs/sancha\" class=\"wiki-link\">Doña Sancha of Kordava</a>, keeping her captive in his gilded cabin as both his mistress and a living trophy of his defiance of the High Alcázar. While he treats her with flamboyant, courtly extravagance, she lives in constant peril of his explosive, jealous rages.</p>\n\n<div class=\"info-card\">\n<h4>Strategic Importance to the Triumvirate</h4>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Naval Counter-Weight:</strong> While <a href=\"#npcs/valenza\" class=\"wiki-link\">General Valenza</a> relies on mercenary cogs and <a href=\"#npcs/tiberio\" class=\"wiki-link\">Ambassador Tiberio</a> uses the <a href=\"#factions/argossean-grain-fleet\" class=\"wiki-link\">Argossean Grain Fleet</a> to strangle royal shipping, Zaporavo's <em>Wastrel</em> rules the coastal reefs. If the PC Triumvirate can secure his privateering allegiance, the <em>Wastrel</em> can break the grain blockade or raid Argossean supply lines with impunity.</li>\n  <li><strong>Secret Anchorage in Baracha:</strong> Zaporavo knows the uncharted shoals of the Barachan Isles, including the lost isle of the Black One and hidden supply caches unknown to the crown admiralty.</li>\n  <li><strong>The Dueling Trap:</strong> Because Zaporavo cannot ignore an insult to his honor, an antagonistic PC duelist can provoke him into a formal dawn duel on the sands of an isolated spit, bypassing an entire crew of 60 boarding cutthroats.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"gm-callout\">\n<div class=\"gm-badge\">GM CONFIDENTIAL &bull; ZAPORAVO'S LETTERS OF MARQUE</div>\n<p>Zaporavo secretly holds a faded royal patent granted during Period VII by the rebel faction, granting him lawful rights to pillage crown loyalists. He despises <a href=\"#npcs/zarono\" class=\"wiki-link\">Captain Black Zarono</a>, whom he considers an unprincipled butcher lacking true chivalric blood. If the PCs promise to restore his family's confiscated vineyards in the <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#gazetteer/zingg-valley\">Zingg Valley</a>, Zaporavo will turn his cannons against <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#npcs/zarono\">Zarono</a> and the Argossean navy.</p>\n</div>\n",
      "gmSecrets": "Zaporavo keeps an ornate iron chest beneath his bunk containing navigational charts of the Western Ocean and private love-letters between Doña Sancha and a high minister of the Restoration Council.",
