      "aliases": [
        "Lady Belesa",
        "Belesa of Korzetta",
        "Belesa",
        "The Defiant Lady",
        "Heiress of Korzetta",
        "Doña Belesa"
      ],
      "summary": "The fiercely courageous niece and rightful heir to Count Valenso of Korzetta. Standing firm against the madness of her uncle, the threats of invading Pictish war-bands, and the predatory advances of Captain Black Zarono, Belesa represents the untarnished honor of old Zingaran nobility.",
      "atAGlance": {
        "Visual Appearance": "A young noblewoman of slender, athletic grace, with thick chestnut hair, steady grey eyes, and noble features. Dresses in practical leather riding skirts and a woolen mantle, wearing a slender steel rapier at her hip with natural familiarity.",
        "Demeanor & Mannerisms": "Calm, protective, and resolute. Refuses to display panic even under pirate bombardment; speaks with quiet, unshakeable authority; fiercest when defending her young ward Tina.",
        "Combat Style": "6th-Level Fighter/Noble. Skilled in Zingaran rapier fencing (1d8+2 damage) and horseback archery. Fights with discipline and tactical courage.",
        "Social Lever": "A passionate commitment to save her household retainers from slaughter and reclaim her family's ancestral fief from corrupt court usurpers."
      },
      "content": "\n<div class=\"npc-header-card\">\n  <div class=\"npc-meta\">\n    <span class=\"badge faction-badge\"><a href=\"#factions/grandees\" class=\"wiki-link\">Grandee Coalitions</a> / Loyalists</span>\n    <span class=\"badge rival-badge\">Rivals: <a href=\"#npcs/zarono\" class=\"wiki-link\">Captain Black Zarono</a> & <a href=\"#npcs/sadoria\" class=\"wiki-link\">Marquis Murzio de Sadoria</a></span>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"at-a-glance-grid\">\n    <div class=\"glance-item\"><strong>Visual Appearance:</strong> Striking young noblewoman with thick dark hair, steady grey eyes, and proud posture, dressed in sea-faring riding leathers with a silver-pommeled rapier.</div>\n    <div class=\"glance-item\"><strong>Demeanor & Mannerisms:</strong> Dignified, unflinching, and fiercely protective of her dependents. She stands up to her uncle's hysterical fits and sneers at pirate demands.</div>\n    <div class=\"glance-item\"><strong>Combat Style:</strong> 6th-Level Fighter/Fencer. AC 3 (studded leather, high DEX), Rapier +1, 1d8+2 damage. Excellent moral courage (Morale 10).</div>\n    <div class=\"glance-item\"><strong>Social Lever:</strong> Sovereign Justice. If the PC Triumvirate offers royal protection and validates her legal claim to the <a href=\"#gazetteer/fief-of-korzetta\" class=\"wiki-link\">Fief of Korzetta</a>, Belesa will become the crown's most loyal champion among the western nobility.</div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<h3>Dossier & Narrative Lore</h3>\n<p><strong>The Courage of the House of <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#gazetteer/fief-of-korzetta\">Korzetta</a>.</strong> While her uncle, <a href=\"#npcs/valenso-korzetta\" class=\"wiki-link\">Count Valenso</a>, descended into shrieking paranoia and occult ruin, Lady Belesa emerged as the true anchor of the <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#gazetteer/fief-of-korzetta\">Korzetta</a> household. In Robert E. Howard's <em>\"The Black Stranger\"</em>, she is the emotional and moral center of the drama, shielding her little handmaid Tina from Pictish arrows and flatly refusing the blackmailing marriage proposals of the predatory buccaneer <a href=\"#npcs/zarono\" class=\"wiki-link\">Captain Black Zarono</a>.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Battle for the Western Marches.</strong> If brought back to Zingara, Lady Belesa represents a seismic political opportunity for the PC Triumvirate. As the indisputable legitimate heir to the <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#gazetteer/fief-of-korzetta\">County of Korzetta</a>, her word carries tremendous weight among the western <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#factions/grandees\">Grandees</a>, who currently distrust both <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#npcs/valenza\">General Valenza</a>'s military occupation and Marquis Sadoria's tax collectors. Backing Belesa allows the PCs to install an honorable, loyal vassal over a crucial maritime region.</p>\n\n<div class=\"info-card\">\n<h4>Political Significance at the High Alcázar</h4>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Defying <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#npcs/zarono\">Zarono</a>'s Ambitions:</strong> <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#npcs/zarono\">Captain Black Zarono</a> has vowed to force Belesa to the altar in order to seize the title of Count of <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#gazetteer/fief-of-korzetta\">Korzetta</a> by marriage. Sponsoring Belesa gives the PCs a casus belli to crush <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#npcs/zarono\">Zarono</a>'s privateering syndicate.</li>\n  <li><strong>Peasant Loyalty:</strong> The tenant farmers and fishermen of <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#gazetteer/fief-of-korzetta\">Korzetta</a> adore Belesa for her compassion during the civil war. Her return would immediately end civil tax resistance throughout the western bluffs.</li>\n  <li><strong>Chivalric <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#overview/pundonor\">Pundonor</a>:</strong> A PC warrior who champions Belesa in a duel against <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#npcs/zarono\">Zarono</a> or an encroaching Grandee earns massive <em>pundonor</em> standing across all chivalric orders of Zingara.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n",
      "gmSecrets": "Belesa managed to smuggle the Great Seal of Korzetta out of the castle before their flight, hidden inside the hollow hilt of her rapier. Without this seal, no edict transferring Korzetta lands is legally binding under Zingaran chivalric law.",
