      "aliases": [
        "Beloso",
        "Beloso the Scout",
        "Beloso the Agile",
        "Beloso of Valbroso",
        "The Shadow of the Pass"
      ],
      "summary": "A lean, wiry, wolf-eyed Zingaran border scout and garrison captain formerly stationed at Castle Valbroso. The only living man who has mapped every treacherous trail through the ghoul-haunted southern border forests into the Kingdom of Argos, Beloso is an opportunistic mercenary whose knowledge is worth a king's ransom.",
      "atAGlance": {
        "Visual Appearance": "Lean, wiry, and sinewy, with narrow hawk-like eyes, scarred forearms, and a ragged dark beard. Wears supple boiled-leather brigandine studded with tarnished steel, high soft-leather riding boots, and a hooded woodland mantle.",
        "Demeanor & Mannerisms": "Perpetually alert; walks without making a sound even on dry gravel. Speaks in a low, gravelly whisper; glances constantly toward trees and tree-lines for ambushes.",
        "Combat Style": "8th-Level Thief/Ranger (DEX 18, CON 14, WIS 15). AC 2 (DEX bonus & brigandine); deadly with short composite bow (+8 to hit, 1d6+2) and twin curved Zingaran daggers (1d4+3, backstab x3).",
        "Social Lever": "Cold hard coin and royal pardons. Beloso has deserted two different noble garrisons and knows he is a marked man unless protected by the highest royal authority."
      },
      "content": "\n<div class=\"npc-header-card\">\n  <div class=\"npc-meta\">\n    <span class=\"badge faction-badge\">Borderland Scouts / Unaligned</span>\n    <span class=\"badge rival-badge\">Former Master: <a href=\"#npcs/count-valbroso\" class=\"wiki-link\">Count Valbroso</a></span>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"at-a-glance-grid\">\n    <div class=\"glance-item\"><strong>Visual Appearance:</strong> Lean, wiry scout in studded leather brigandine and dark hooded mantle, equipped with composite recurve bow and paired border dirks.</div>\n    <div class=\"glance-item\"><strong>Demeanor & Mannerisms:</strong> Silent, watchful, and deeply pragmatic. He trusts terrain over men and steel over words; speaks only when he has vital information to sell.</div>\n    <div class=\"glance-item\"><strong>Combat Style:</strong> 8th-Level Scout/Thief. Master of woodland ambush and concealment (Hide in Shadows 85%, Move Silently 90%). Backstab damage x3.</div>\n    <div class=\"glance-item\"><strong>Social Lever:</strong> A royal pardon stamped with the High Seal, absolving him of treason charges from <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#gazetteer/castle-valbroso\">Castle Valbroso</a> and guaranteeing safe passage in <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#gazetteer/kordava\">Kordava</a>.</div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<h3>Dossier & Narrative Lore</h3>\n<p><strong>The Ghost of the Border Woods.</strong> In Chapter 12 and 13 of Robert E. Howard's canonical masterpiece <em>The Hour of the Dragon</em>, Beloso appears as the cunning, quick-witted soldier-at-arms in <a href=\"#gazetteer/castle-valbroso\" class=\"wiki-link\">Castle Valbroso</a>. When chaos engulfed the fortress over the stolen Heart of Ahriman, Beloso was the opportunist who struck from the shadows, seized the prize, and vanished like smoke into the night, outriding king and warriors alike across the rugged hills of southern Zingara.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Only Guide Through the Ghoul Woods.</strong> Today, Beloso operates as an independent scout along the perilous border between Zingara and the <a href=\"#gazetteer/kingdom-of-argos\" class=\"wiki-link\">Kingdom of Argos</a>. The vast, dark forests of the southern border (the <a href=\"#gazetteer/forest-of-ghouls\" class=\"wiki-link\">Forest of Ghouls</a>) are notorious across the Hyborian world for packs of man-eating ghouls, bloodthirsty brigands, and ancient ruins. Beloso is one of only two men who know the secret cattle paths and smugglers' tracks that bypass the haunted barrows and lead directly to the Argossean highway toward Messantia.</p>\n\n<div class=\"info-card\">\n<h4>Utility to the PC Triumvirate</h4>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Infiltrating <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#gazetteer/castle-valbroso\">Castle Valbroso</a>:</strong> Beloso served five years as postern-guard at <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#gazetteer/castle-valbroso\">Castle Valbroso</a>. He knows the secret drainage sluices and forgotten tunnels that lead directly beneath <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#npcs/count-valbroso\">Count Valbroso</a>'s torture chambers.</li>\n  <li><strong>Overland Courier to <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#factions/foreign-powers\">Argos</a>:</strong> If Kordova's port is blockaded by <a href=\"#npcs/nikolos-voros\" class=\"wiki-link\">Nikolos Voros</a> or pirate fleets, Beloso can guide royal couriers through the border forest into <a class=\"wiki-link\" href=\"#factions/foreign-powers\">Argos</a> in under four days, bypassing all royal army checkpoints.</li>\n  <li><strong>Relic Hunter:</strong> Beloso has explored several forgotten Acheronian crypts buried in the border hills and knows the location of trapped chests containing pre-Cataclysmic jewels.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n",
      "gmSecrets": "Beloso carries a map drawn on human skin showing the exact lair of the Ghoul-King in the southern forest, where an ancient king's signet ring lies among gnawed bones.",
